    <!-- NEW: YAML Anchors & Aliases -->
    <section class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50 mb-3 text-center">Understanding YAML Anchors &amp; Aliases in Conversion</h2>
      <p class="text-center text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 mb-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">YAML anchors and aliases let you reuse values across your document. During conversion to JSON, all references are fully expanded — the output contains the actual values, not the references.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="px-4 py-2 bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 border-b border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-700 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">YAML with Anchors</span>
          </div>
          <pre id="anc-yaml" class="p-4 text-sm font-mono"></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="px-4 py-2 bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 border-b border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-700 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-blue-500"></span>
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">JSON — Fully Expanded</span>
          </div>
          <pre id="anc-json" class="p-4 text-sm font-mono"></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-800/60 bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/20">
        <p class="text-sm text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-300"><strong>Key insight:</strong> JSON has no equivalent for YAML anchors. The <code class="text-xs px-1 py-0.5 rounded bg-amber-100 dark:bg-amber-900/40">&amp;defaults</code> anchor and <code class="text-xs px-1 py-0.5 rounded bg-amber-100 dark:bg-amber-900/40">*defaults</code> alias are resolved into actual values. The merge key <code class="text-xs px-1 py-0.5 rounded bg-amber-100 dark:bg-amber-900/40">&lt;&lt;</code> is also expanded. This means the JSON output may be larger than the YAML source — but the data is identical.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- NEW: Best Practices -->
    <section class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50 mb-3 text-center">Best Practices for YAML to JSON Conversion</h2>
      <p class="text-center text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 mb-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">Follow these guidelines to ensure smooth, error-free conversion every time.</p>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="flex gap-4 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80">
          <span class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/30 text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 font-bold text-sm">1</span>
          <div><h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1">Validate YAML Before Converting</h3><p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Always check your YAML for syntax errors first. Use the YAML Formatter tab to validate and fix indentation issues before switching to the JSON conversion tab.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80">
          <span class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/30 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-400 font-bold text-sm">2</span>
          <div><h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1">Use Spaces, Never Tabs</h3><p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">YAML strictly forbids tab characters for indentation. Use 2 spaces per level for the cleanest, most portable YAML. Most editors have a "convert tabs to spaces" option.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80">
          <span class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/30 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-400 font-bold text-sm">3</span>
          <div><h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1">Quote Ambiguous Values</h3><p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">If a value like <code class="text-xs px-1 py-0.5 rounded bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800">yes</code>, <code class="text-xs px-1 py-0.5 rounded bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800">no</code>, <code class="text-xs px-1 py-0.5 rounded bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800">on</code>, or <code class="text-xs px-1 py-0.5 rounded bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800">off</code> should be a string (not a boolean), always wrap it in quotes in your YAML source.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80">
          <span class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-amber-100 dark:bg-amber-900/30 text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 font-bold text-sm">4</span>
          <div><h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1">Keep Nesting Reasonable</h3><p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Deeply nested YAML is hard to read and error-prone. When you exceed 4-5 levels of nesting, consider breaking the structure into separate files or using YAML anchors to reduce repetition.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80">
          <span class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-100 dark:bg-red-900/30 text-red-700 dark:text-red-400 font-bold text-sm">5</span>
          <div><h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1">Plan for Comment Loss</h3><p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Since JSON drops all comments, move important documentation to a README file or use descriptive key names in your YAML. This preserves context that would otherwise be lost in conversion.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

