    <section class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50 mb-8 text-center">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <dl class="space-y-2">
        <div class="border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
          <dt><button type="button" class="faq-toggle flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-4 text-left text-sm font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 hover:bg-zinc-50 dark:hover:bg-zinc-900/50 transition-colors" aria-expanded="false"><span>Is the YAML to JSON conversion accurate?</span><svg class="faq-chevron w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></button></dt>
          <dd class="faq-answer hidden px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">Yes. We use the <code class="text-xs">yaml</code> library (v2) which follows the YAML 1.2 specification. All data types, nested structures, and values are preserved exactly during conversion. The conversion is fully lossless.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
          <dt><button type="button" class="faq-toggle flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-4 text-left text-sm font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 hover:bg-zinc-50 dark:hover:bg-zinc-900/50 transition-colors" aria-expanded="false"><span>Does this tool send my data to a server?</span><svg class="faq-chevron w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></button></dt>
          <dd class="faq-answer hidden px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">No. All YAML to JSON conversion runs entirely in your browser using client-side JavaScript. Your data never leaves your computer. You can disconnect from the internet and the converter will continue to work.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
          <dt><button type="button" class="faq-toggle flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-4 text-left text-sm font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 hover:bg-zinc-50 dark:hover:bg-zinc-900/50 transition-colors" aria-expanded="false"><span>Does it handle YAML anchors and aliases?</span><svg class="faq-chevron w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></button></dt>
          <dd class="faq-answer hidden px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">Yes. YAML anchors (<code class="text-xs">&amp;</code>) and aliases (<code class="text-xs">*</code>) are fully resolved during conversion. The resulting JSON contains the expanded, actual values — not the anchor references. Merge keys (<code class="text-xs">&lt;&lt;</code>) are also supported.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
          <dt><button type="button" class="faq-toggle flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-4 text-left text-sm font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 hover:bg-zinc-50 dark:hover:bg-zinc-900/50 transition-colors" aria-expanded="false"><span>Can I convert large YAML files?</span><svg class="faq-chevron w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></button></dt>
          <dd class="faq-answer hidden px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">Yes. The tool handles files with thousands of lines efficiently. For extremely large files (10,000+ lines), conversion may take a moment but remains fully client-side. You can also drag and drop <code class="text-xs">.yaml</code> or <code class="text-xs">.yml</code> files directly into the editor.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
          <dt><button type="button" class="faq-toggle flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-4 text-left text-sm font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 hover:bg-zinc-50 dark:hover:bg-zinc-900/50 transition-colors" aria-expanded="false"><span>What happens to YAML comments during conversion?</span><svg class="faq-chevron w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></button></dt>
          <dd class="faq-answer hidden px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">Comments are dropped during conversion because JSON does not support comments. This is by design — the JSON specification has no comment syntax. If you need to preserve documentation, consider adding descriptive key names in your YAML before converting.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
          <dt><button type="button" class="faq-toggle flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-4 text-left text-sm font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 hover:bg-zinc-50 dark:hover:bg-zinc-900/50 transition-colors" aria-expanded="false"><span>How are YAML data types mapped to JSON?</span><svg class="faq-chevron w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></button></dt>
          <dd class="faq-answer hidden px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">YAML strings, numbers, booleans (<code class="text-xs">true</code>/<code class="text-xs">false</code>), and null map directly to JSON equivalents. YAML sequences (lists) become JSON arrays. YAML mappings become JSON objects. YAML dates are converted to ISO 8601 strings.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>
  </main>

